WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.357
Let’s bring the main ideas together.

00:00:02.357 --> 00:00:05.497
Variables give names to values.

00:00:05.497 --> 00:00:09.467
Data types tell Python what those values mean.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:16.767
Arithmetic creates derived metrics. Formatting helps us communicate results clearly.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:21.722
Type conversion helps when data arrives in the wrong form for calculation.

00:00:22.459 --> 00:00:30.881
The larger pattern is simple: store the data, understand its type, transform it, and communicate the result.

00:00:30.881 --> 00:00:37.662
Next, we add decisions and repetition with if statements, for loops, and while loops.

00:00:38.117 --> 00:00:46.464
In Module 2, we’ll build directly on this foundation by giving Python the ability to make decisions and repeat work.

00:00:46.464 --> 00:00:53.459
You’ll use conditions, if statements, for loops, and while loops to classify values, apply rules,

00:00:53.459 --> 00:00:58.039
and process more than one observation at a time.

00:00:58.039 --> 00:01:03.259
That is where your programs begin to behave more like real analytical workflows.
